This series is now at v7 with 7 patches (initial P8700 SoC support, Boston
board support, EG20T GPIO driver, PCI Xilinx root-port fix, MIPS GIC syscon
driver, pch_gbe PHY reset/MAC fallback, and CM/IOCU support), and patch
01/07 already has a Reviewed-by from Leo Yu-Chi Liang, but across 7
revisions there do not appear to be any Reviewed-by/Acked-by tags
accumulated from a second maintainer, nor any visible sign-off from a
RISC-V or MIPS subsystem maintainer beyond the co-author (Chao-ying Fu).

Given the revision count, could a maintainer (Leo Liang / Rick Chen /
Tom Rini) confirm whether this series is actively blocked on something
specific (e.g. awaiting hardware validation, pending comments not yet
addressed, or simply queue backlog), since v7 with effectively single-
reviewer engagement after this many iterations suggests it may need
explicit maintainer attention to either merge or identify what's still
missing before it can be picked up.

On patch 01/07 itself (arch/riscv/cpu/p8700/cache.c): the cache_loop() macro
forces the address operand into register a0 via a fixed-register asm
constraint to encode a custom MCACHE instruction - has this been tested on
actual P8700 silicon (hart0 GCR/CM programming path plus the per-hart PMP/
PMA setup in harts_early_init()), or only in simulation? That early-init
path runs before DRAM is up and is easy to get subtly wrong without
hardware in hand.
